Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:51:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/40] Steady-state detection: TS_LOCAL, so that it runs with
 the neighbour flags

The steady-state detection kept the barriers: it recorded its E-field probes in a ring of two periods, and the
evaluation of a period (by the thread that copies the last lines) assumed every thread at the same timestep.
With the flags a thread can be up to the thread count of timesteps ahead of another, so the ring now keeps
three periods (the record of timestep TS at TS mod 3p) and an evaluation reads the last two periods by
timestep (slot k of the two-period ring is the last timestep <= TS with that slot). While a period is longer
than twice the thread count, no thread reaches the next evaluation step or overwrites a record of the last
two periods before the evaluation of this one is done, and the copies and the count of copied lines are not
touched in between: GetUsedHooks() declares TS_LOCAL then. Same records, same sums in the same order
(bit-identical); upstream's GPU engines use the extension's energy and change only, not its records.

Verified: the steady-state boxes (Mur, PML, lumped RLC, conducting sheets, Drude, Debye, a delayed and a
soft H excitation, 3000-30000 steps) with a trace of every period evaluation: fields, probe, trace and stop
step identical to the sse-compressed engine at 1, 3, 4, 8 and 10 threads (flags in 28 of 56 runs), stop step
and probe identical to stock v0.37.0. Upstream's cases against the previous commit (barriers), paired
interleaved A/B, 5 rounds: ideal (1 M cells, 3000 steps) x1.18 at 8 threads and x1.13 with the automatic
count, ideal M (8 M cells, 600 steps) x1.07 and x1.05, inhomogeneous x1.41 and pml x1.05 at 8 threads (under
1.5-3 cores of other load), dispersive within the noise (under 3 cores of other load).

